  "description": "<p>Currently the only way to re-use a URI in Fedora is to delete &amp; purge the URI. Then PUT a new object at that URI.</p>\n\n<p>With <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3881\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3881</a> we are disallowing this pattern for parts of an Archival Group which prevents the re-use of a URI without deleting the entire object.</p>\n\n<p>This ticket is to consider whether we should and if we do, how we might implement the ability to PUT over a tombstone to recreate the object.</p>\n\n<p>Considerations:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>We would need a check to ensure the PUT is understood to be re-creating the object. i.e. some header must be included.</li>\n\t<li>This PUT would be considered part of the previously deleted object, so there would be no change to interaction model allowed.</li>\n\t<li>The previous version history of the object would also be maintained.</li>\n\t<li>The previous version history of the object would contain versions where the version was DELETEd and you will get a 410 Gone</li>\n</ul>\n",
